SUMMARY:CMHC Peer Groups (FolkTime × Clackamas County): ColorFlow
DESCRIPTION:Category: Peer Support\nCost: FREE\nFormat: In-person\nInfo: Pe
 er-led with Luna. A welcoming art group for creative self-expression and m
 indfulness through paint. Explore emotions\, connect with others\, and fin
 d calm through color. No art experience needed.\nAddress: 11211 SE 82nd Av
 e\, Suite O\, Portland\, OR 97086\nPhone: 503-722-6200\nWebsite: https://f
 olktime.org\nDetails: Peer-led creative\, mindful\, and connection-focused
  groups at Clackamas Mental Health Clinic\, offered through FolkTime in pa
 rtnership with Clackamas County. Groups return August 2026 after a hiatus\
 , with a revised line-up — ColorFlow moved from Wednesdays to Tuesdays\, C
 ultivate & Connect is now Inspired by Nature\, Karaoke Night is now Open M
 ic Night\, and Tea Time and Fun Brain Food are new. Verified from the offi
 cial FolkTime/Clackamas County flyer received July 2026.
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC "-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//EN"><HTML><BODY><p><strong>Category:</strong> Peer Support</p><p><strong>Cost:</strong> FREE</p><p><strong>Format:</strong> In-person</p><p>Peer-led with Luna. A welcoming art group for creative self-expression and mindfulness through paint. Explore emotions, connect with others, and find calm through color. No art experience needed.</p><p><strong>Address:</strong> 11211 SE 82nd Ave, Suite O, Portland, OR 97086</p><p><strong>Phone:</strong> <a href="tel:503-722-6200">503-722-6200</a></p><p><strong>Website:</strong> <a href="https://folktime.org">https://folktime.org</a></p><p><strong>Details:</strong> Peer-led creative, mindful, and connection-focused groups at Clackamas Mental Health Clinic, offered through FolkTime in partnership with Clackamas County. Groups return August 2026 after a hiatus, with a revised line-up — ColorFlow moved from Wednesdays to Tuesdays, Cultivate &amp; Connect is now Inspired by Nature, Karaoke Night is now Open Mic Night, and Tea Time and Fun Brain Food are new. Verified from the official FolkTime/Clackamas County flyer received July 2026.</p></BODY></HTML>
