  & Meditation
DESCRIPTION:Category: Peer Support\nCost: FREE\nFormat: In-person\nInfo: Pe
 er-led with Alé. A peaceful\, grounding space to slow down\, breathe\, and
  reconnect with yourself. Together we'll explore stillness\, mindfulness\,
  and the power of silence as a way to rest\, reflect\, and find calm in co
 mmunity.\nAddress: 11211 SE 82nd Ave\, Suite O\, Portland\, OR 97086\nPhon
 e: 503-722-6200\nWebsite: https://folktime.org\nDetails: Peer-led creative
 \, mindful\, and connection-focused groups at Clackamas Mental Health Clin
 ic\, offered through FolkTime in partnership with Clackamas County. Groups
  return August 2026 after a hiatus\, with a revised line-up — ColorFlow mo
 ved from Wednesdays to Tuesdays\, Cultivate & Connect is now Inspired by N
 ature\, Karaoke Night is now Open Mic Night\, and Tea Time and Fun Brain F
 ood are new. Verified from the official FolkTime/Clackamas County flyer re
 ceived July 2026.
